## Dependency Table (deterministic — `check_dependency_rules`)

| # | From | To | Allowed? | Rule ID |
|---|------|----|----------|---------|
| R1 | Trust Foundation | Anything above | FORBIDDEN | DEP.trust_no_upward |
| R2 | Horizontal (services) | Trust Foundation | Yes | DEP.h_reads_trust |
| R4 | Horizontal (services) | Vertical (components) | FORBIDDEN | DEP.h_no_vertical |
| R7 | Vertical | Vertical | FORBIDDEN | DEP.v_no_v |
| R11 | Any | Orchestration | FORBIDDEN | DEP.no_upward_to_orch |
| R12 | Meta | Orchestration | FORBIDDEN | DEP.meta_no_orch (AP-4) |

## Trust Foundation Rules (deterministic — `check_trust_purity`)

- **T1**: `trust/` has zero outward dependencies (Invariant #2).
- **T2**: `trust/` remains pure — no I/O, logging, network (TRUST_PURITY.io_import).
- **T4**: signed vs unsigned metadata boundary respected (re-sign trigger).

## Anti-Patterns (AST where marked)

- **AP-1** trust types inside a service → shared types live in `trust/`.
- **AP-2** horizontal-to-horizontal service coupling.
- **AP-3** hardcoded prompt strings (AST: `detect_anti_patterns`).
- **AP-5** orchestration node with domain logic (not a thin wrapper).
- **AP-6** Pydantic BaseModel defined in `utils/`/`services/` (AST).

## Frontend deterministic predicates (TS — `code_reviewer/frontend/tools.py`)

- `check_csp_strict`, `check_iframe_sandbox`, `check_secrets_in_public_env`,
  `check_jwt_storage`, `check_composer_keyboard`. These run first for TS/TSX files
  and their PASS/FAIL takes precedence over LLM judgment.

## ADR Ratchet (Track C — root `REVIEW.md` ADR.1)

A diff matching an `⚠️ Ask first` trigger (new `pyproject.toml` dependency,
`trust/models.py` change, new node in `orchestration/react_loop.py`, or a new
horizontal service) with **no** new file under `docs/adr/` → flag **ADR.1**
(warning, D2). This is mechanically checkable from the changed-file list.

